.TH SHMCTL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
shmctl \- control a System V shared memory segment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/shm.h>
.B int shmctl(int id, int command, struct shmid_ds* buffer);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
IPC_STAT reads segment metadata into buffer; IPC_SET updates permitted fields;
IPC_RMID marks a segment for removal. SHM_LOCK and SHM_UNLOCK request Linux
locking operations. Pass NULL when the command requires no buffer.
The supplied structures use Linux x86\-64 layouts and are not portable.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shmget (3crunch),
.BR shmdt (3crunch),
.BR shmctl (2)
